<title>UK: Watson &amp; Philip falls after profit warning.</title>
<headline>Watson &amp; Philip falls after profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Watson &amp; Philip shares fell 38-1/2 pence to 427-1/2 after the food distributor and retailer issued a profit warning, which will likely be followed by analysts lowering their results estimates, dealers said.</p>
<p>Watson &amp; Philip said its full-year profit before property and execptional items would come in at the lower end of market expectations.</p>
<p>Market forecasts varied between 18.5 and 21.8 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;I will imagine there will some downgradings,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
